// =====================================================================================
//  IDOLVERSE48: Select Bloom! — BLOOM: THE IDOL PROJECT (annual survival show)
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  One season per in-game year, titled "BLOOM: THE IDOL PROJECT <year>"  ·  S.bloom.seasons[year]
//   March 1–31   applications: members decide for themselves whether to apply; the company approves or rejects
//                (shared company quota of 10). A member with any company commitment between April 1 and EP.13
//                (theater, events, releases, concerts, roadshows, bookings…) is ineligible and cannot be approved.
//   April 1      the season starts: 60 contestants (approved members + generated contestants from other agencies,
//                generated once and saved). Company contestants are unavailable for company work until EP.13.
//   Sundays      13 weekly episodes (April → June). Each episode is processed on its broadcast day and saved:
//                results, rankings, events, and the still images of every company contestant (scene recipes drawn
//                from her own character art, so reopening an episode always shows the same images).
//   EP.13        final ranking; 7–12 debut members (decided by the final result, never shown in advance) form a
//                Project Group — a real group of the company with its own team, releases, concerts, TV and awards —
//                for exactly two years. Members leave their original group activities for the contract and return
//                afterwards (original contract rules A/B/C). Every company contestant gains new fans through the
//                existing fan system (unique fans, Kami Oshi / Oshi supporters, worldwide fans).
//  Performance (skill) scores and vote scores are kept separately; the rank score combines them.
// =====================================================================================
